Final file:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;

public static class NativeCompression
{
    [DllImport("compresslib", CallingConvention = CallingConvention.Cdecl,
        EntryPoint = "compress_buffer", ExactSpelling = true)]
    public static extern int CompressBuffer(
        [In] byte[] input,
        UIntPtr inputLen,
        [Out] byte[] output,
        UIntPtr outputLen,
        out UIntPtr bytesWritten);
}
```

Key choices:
- **`EntryPoint`** explicitly names the native symbol so the C# method can use PascalCase.
- **`UIntPtr`** correctly represents `size_t` (32-bit on x86 .NET Framework).
- **`Cdecl`** prevents stack corruption since the C function uses the C calling convention.
